            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Equal arc lengths give radii in the ratio 3:4; circle areas are proportional to the squares of their radii.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let the radii of $C_1$ and $C_2$ be $r_1$ and $r_2$. The arcs are respectively one-sixth and one-eighth of their circles.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac16(2\\pi r_1)&=\\frac18(2\\pi r_2)\\\\8r_1&=6r_2\\\\\\frac{r_1}{r_2}&=\\frac34\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $A=\\pi r^2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}A_1:A_2&=\\pi r_1^2:\\pi r_2^2\\\\A_1:A_2&=3^2:4^2\\\\A_1:A_2&=9:16\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
